## 4. Security and privacy (mandatory)

- **`UriValidator` before every stat/open/hash:** API-only URI resolution; grant boundary under active `scan_root`; authority allowlist; **fail-closed** → `PERMISSION_DENIED`; **no** `..` in SAF docId; **do not follow** symlinks.
- **`RedactionFilter`** on all strings to crash SDK, opt-in analytics, and JS bridge errors (denylist patterns 1–7 in architecture §8.2). On-screen paths for the user are allowed; telemetry egress is not.
- **Hash phase:** Read-only FDs only — no write/truncate/delete syscalls.
- **Delete phase:** `DeleteCoordinator` only, isolated from hash FD pool.
- **Prod:** `frame_hashes_blob` debug-only; never in crash/analytics (AC-security-blob-01).
- **Analytics:** Opt-in, **default off**. Allowed telemetry fields only per architecture §8.2.

---

## 5. Data model and schema

- Implement tables and columns per `docs/architecture.md` §5. Do not invent parallel stores (AsyncStorage catalog, second DB, in-memory-only index for production paths).
- **`schema_version`** in `meta` is independent of app semver. Bump → set `full_rescan_required` → `RescanPromptBanner`. **Do not** support app downgrade across schema migrations.
- **Unscannable reason codes (closed set):** `CLOUD_PLACEHOLDER`, `ENCRYPTED`, `PERMISSION_DENIED`, `OFFLINE_ONLY`, `LOCKED`, `LARGE_SKIPPED`, `HASH_TIMEOUT`, `VIDEO_DECODE_FAILED`. Never skip silently (FR-UN-01).
- **Hard links:** Same inode+device → one `file_entry_id`, multiple `file_path` alias rows.

