### VideoFingerprinter (M1-13)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.hash.VideoFingerprinter`, `DHash`, `VideoContentMatcher`, `VideoFingerprintCodec`; injectable `VideoFrameExtractor`; `AndroidVideoMetadataReader` on StatStage for video rows.
- **iOS:** `DBVideoFingerprinter`, `DBDHash`, `DBVideoContentMatcher`, `DBVideoFingerprint` under `ScanEngine/Hash/`.
- **Pipeline:** Video files hash `RAW_BYTES` + `VIDEO_CONTENT_V1` in parallel (`HashResult.VideoSuccess` / `DBHashPipelineOutcomeVideoSuccess`); >500 MB without opt-in skips content fingerprint (`VideoPartialSuccess`).
- **Caps:** 90 s wall-clock, 500 MB budget (2 GB with `largeFilesOptIn`), 5-frame dHash at 2/25/50/75/98% (single frame <3 s), Hamming ≤8 default, duration gate (2% and <1 s delta).
- **Index:** `fingerprint_id` = VIDEO_CONTENT_V1, `raw_content_fingerprint_id` = RAW_BYTES on `file_entry`; `frame_hashes_blob` on fingerprint row (debug-only egress).
- **Grouper:** EXACT_BYTES via `raw_content_fingerprint_id`; SAME_CONTENT_VIDEO via `fingerprint_id` profile; fuzzy Hamming clustering for M1-18 fixture suite uses `VideoContentMatcher`.
- **Tests:** `DHashTest`, `VideoFingerprinterTest`, `VideoContentMatcherTest`, `VideoFingerprintCodecTest` / iOS `DBVideoFingerprinterTests`, `DBVideoContentMatcherTests`; fixture `hash-video-content-01.json`.
- **Platform decoders:** Production `MediaCodec` / `AVAssetReader` frame extractors are wired when scan orchestrator lands; M1-13 ships algorithm + injectable extractor + unit tests.

### Video pipeline exception (M1-14)

- **Android:** `DurationBucketIndex`, `InMemoryDurationBucketIndex`, `SqliteDurationBucketIndex`; `HashPipeline` runs duration pre-bucket before size-bucket for video.
- **iOS:** `DBDurationBucketIndex`, `DBInMemoryDurationBucketIndex`, `DBSqliteDurationBucketIndex`; same ordering in `DBHashPipeline`.
- **Size-bucket skip:** Video never size-bucket-skips (`SizeBucketIndex` / `DBSizeBucketIndex` always `NEEDS_HASH`); `countIndexedFilesWithSize` excludes rows with `duration_ms > 0`.
- **Duration pre-bucket:** Registers `duration_ms` from StatStage before size-bucket; disposition is informational (`UNIQUE_DURATION` / `HAS_GATE_CANDIDATE` / `DURATION_UNKNOWN`) — video always runs `RAW_BYTES` + `VIDEO_CONTENT_V1` (FR-FP-02 / FR-FP-07).
- **Tests:** `DurationBucketIndexTest`, `HashPipelineTest` (AC-pipeline-video-01); fixture `pipeline/hash-pipeline-video-01.json`.

### Schema v2 migration (M1-15)

- **Android:** `CatalogMigrator`, `CatalogSchema.applyLegacyV1Schema`; `CatalogDatabase.onUpgrade` → v1→v2 ALTER + `full_rescan_required=1`; clears `duplicate_group` / `duplicate_member`.
- **iOS:** `DBCatalogMigrator`, `DBCatalogSchema legacyV1*` DDL; `DBCatalogDatabase` runs migration when `meta.schema_version` &lt; current.
- **Index:** `upsertVideoPartialHashed` persists `VIDEO_DECODE_FAILED` on `file_entry.unscannable_reason` while keeping `RAW_BYTES` fingerprint (AC-unscan-06 / AC-security-decode-01).
- **`match_kind`:** Already written by `Grouper` / `DBGrouper` (`EXACT_BYTES` / `SAME_CONTENT_VIDEO`); migration adds column with default `EXACT_BYTES` for legacy rows then clears groups for rescan.
- **Tests:** `CatalogMigratorTest`, `IndexWriterTest` (video partial); iOS `DBCatalogMigratorTests`, `DBIndexWriterTests`; fixtures `index-schema-migration-01.json`, `security-decode-01.json`.

