## 11. Banned approaches (do not propose or implement)

### Stack and platform

| Banned | Why | Use instead |
|--------|-----|-------------|
| Expo managed workflow | No unconstrained FGS + custom Turbo Module | Bare RN |
| `MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` | Play policy / scope | MediaStore + SAF Mode A/B |
| Cloud upload hashing | v1 privacy model | On-device ScanEngine only |
| FFmpeg for video v1 | Architecture lock | MediaCodec + MediaExtractor / AVAssetReader |
| BLAKE3 / alternate hash algos | v1 schema lock | SHA-256 + documented `schema_version` bump if ever changed |

### Bridge and data

| Banned | Why | Use instead |
|--------|-----|-------------|
| Sending paths/hashes/bytes over RN bridge | NFR-04, security | Progress + error contract only |
| String path concatenation for URI resolution | TOCTOU / escape risk | Platform APIs + `UriValidator` |
| Following symlinks for duplicate detection | Requirements §4 | Index symlink node only; `is_symlink` |
| JS-thread hashing or SQLite writes for scan path | Performance architecture | Native ScanEngine |
| Second catalog source of truth | FR-IX-01 | Single SQLite index |

### Product scope (defer list — requires new debate)

Do not implement without explicit new consensus: perceptual image near-dupes; cross-format document dedup; symlink follow; filesystem watchers; payload-only A/V hashing; account/backend sync; auto-delete; secure wipe claims; runtime themes; broad `/sdcard` crawl; near-duplicate audio.

### UX and copy

| Banned | Why | Use instead |
|--------|-----|-------------|
| Paraphrasing frozen EN tokens | Store/a11y freeze | `tokens.ts` literals |
| Auto-selecting keeper on delete | FR-AC-03, AC-action-keeper-01 | Explicit selection + presets |
| Forensic erasure marketing or implementation | FR-SE-05 | Platform default delete semantics |
| FGS notification implying delete/complete early | Play rejection risk | Copy from `notification.*` tokens; complete only when run ends |

